Magi peer into the Dark Wind to understand and alter the hidden fabric of the
world. Your spellbook records that understanding as workings, mastery, runes,
and notes gathered in the field. New pages begin with dependable magic and
grow toward fire, frost, distance, memory, forbidden death-work, and moments
that do not pass until you permit them.

Magi call the art as a whole gramarye and a single spell a working. A working
may be as slight as a cantrip, as patient as a charm, or as cruel as a malison;
the word describes magic made real, not merely the words used to cast it.

Arcane is the guild's rank and rises through Mage GXP. Level-appropriate combat
and useful field casting both advance it. A useful utility working awards 10
GXP, while a useful combat working awards 20, at most once per working every
thirty seconds. A working has its own history as well. Fifty useful casts make it
Practiced, one hundred fifty Fluent, two hundred fifty Inscribed, and one
thousand Instinctive.
Practiced workings gain a rune socket and eligible combat workings can be
prepared with "barrage". Inscribed pages gain a second socket, while deeper
mastery steadily improves efficiency and barrage speed.

Battlemagi wield FOCUS weapons. The weapon channels a known barrage working
beside normal attacks even while that working is still Copied, and those
automatic casts cost no SP. A worn piece of AURA equipment completes the
resonance, adding speed and power. Automatic casts still improve their page and
can earn rate-limited field GXP. "battlemage" shows the exact cadence, cost,
equipment state, and current Recollection timer. Ordinary barrage cadence has
a floor of two combat rounds. Fireball barrage leaves a light Burning effect, Icestorm
barrage reaches nearby hostile targets and Chills them, and Missile lands as a
visible two-missile volley rather than every page using the same impact.

At Arcane 16, preparing a barrage with a real wielded FOCUS trades weapon
swings for a barrage every round. The penalty is one swing below player level
50 and rises by one each fifty levels, reaching six at level 250. Each round
produces two to six complete barrages based on the FOCUS weapon's WC and item
level, not on the Mage's remaining swing count. Investiture cannot enable it.
The battlemage display reduces that combined weapon rating to a short Weave
Power bar, with numeric progress in screen-reader output.

The battlemage style also permits practical shields. Magi may use small and
medium shields of any composition, plus the lightweight wood-and-natural
fighter shield. Large conventional shields and tower shields remain too
restrictive for working magic.

At Arcane 8, "overchannel" can press five percent of maximum SP into each
manual damaging working. Arcane 16 opens ten percent and Arcane 32 opens
twenty percent. Arcane 500 opens twenty-five percent and Arcane 1000 opens
thirty percent. This added cost is not reduced by mastery or Mezari; it becomes
additional spell power and gives deep reserves a deliberate combat use.
The exchange gains another half point of damage per SP for each whole cube-root
step of true Arcane, in addition to effective-rank scaling.
Overchannel lasts for the current play session and never modifies barrage or
automatic echoes.

Traditional spell and guild-level unlocks end at Arcane 15, but Arcane study
itself continues to rank 1000 on a sharply rising cost curve. Ordinary spell
scaling gains only the square root of ranks beyond 32, giving prestige severe
diminishing returns. Marginalia measures that long study cumulatively.

While any cooldown is active, the spellbook has a rare heartbeat chance to
revise every cooldown away at once. This rises from 1 in 10,000 to 25 in
10,000 at Arcane 500 and 100 in 10,000 at Arcane 1000. "mageaura" selects
purely cosmetic prestige effects earned along the way.

Arcane study also cuts through magical resistance, using the same heavily
diminished effective rank after Arcane 32.

At Arcane 4, Investiture can temporarily supply one missing half of that
resonance. "investiture focus" lends FOCUS to an ordinary wielded weapon;
"investiture aura" writes an AURA around the Mage. Only one may be sustained at
a time, which makes the working a bridge into battlemage equipment rather than
a permanent substitute for it.

Recollection appears at Arcane 3. It restores all missing SP after a four-second
weave, costs ten percent of maximum health, and cannot settle during combat. Its
private timer begins at ten minutes. Recollection mastery can remove as much as
four minutes, while FOCUS and AURA each remove another minute; the timer never
falls below five minutes.

Ashkenazy, Falx, Saloman, Talek, James, Rodney, and Aiken are taught through
Arcane study.
Rodney opens at Arcane 7, can only be placed on a buff or control working with
a real duration, and extends it by twenty-five percent through two minutes,
thirty-five percent over two minutes, or fifty percent over five minutes. It
can lengthen concentration blocks, Freezing, and Bodach Powerup, but not Burning. Falx
shortens a bound working's manual cooldown by twenty percent as well as
quickening its barrage cadence. Marsellus, Mezari, and Ravidel reveal
themselves when the spellbook records the right feats of mastery or elemental
practice, but each still has the Arcane threshold shown by "runes". Elemental
and forbidden damage runes add ten percent apiece to the working's primary hit
and merge their damage types into it. Mezari lowers the
inscribed working's SP cost by ten percent. Saloman's damaging return is capped
at one quarter of a manual working's discounted ordinary cost; utility
workings return ten percent of discounted base cost. Free barrage impacts
cannot generate SP.
At Arcane 9, the broken Tower of Arcanarton on the old Isle of the Magi begins
a more dangerous line of research into the Arcanarton and Bodach runes.
Once either pattern is known, a green-spined grimoire in the Darkwind Mage
attic can reveal Trivlian's evil-and-acid rune. James's Whimsy rune gives Mage
Eye and Teleport harmlessly ridiculous manifestations.
Aiken opens at Arcane 8 and can only be bound to damaging workings. It halves
normal armor absorption without bypassing elemental resistance, intrinsic
reduction, shields, or Mana Barrier.

Fireball lands lightly and writes most of its harm into the flames that follow.
Burning may stack to fifty times an NPC's level. Against players it remains
capped at the target's level.

Mana Barrier opens at Arcane 7. While active, each damaging hit has a chance
to spend SP in place of HP after ordinary defenses. Its chance improves with
true Arcane rank, while mastery makes the conversion more efficient.
"battlemage" reports the exact current values.
Concentration blocks pause a prepared barrage without discarding it; the same
cadence resumes when the block lifts. A manual Bolt is independent of the
prepared barrage and scales as a dedicated lightning strike. Bodach changes
Powerup into a guarded fifteen-pulse HP-to-SP buff. Touch uses a fourteen-second
base cooldown. Its final page has unusually deep margins; forbidden runes can
make the working answer to older names, and paired inscriptions do not always
settle for the name either rune would choose alone. Some such workings refuse
to end when the hand draws back.

Useful commands include:

  research / mstudy            Arcane GXP and the next open page
  spells [working]             working index and Arcane thresholds
  spellbook [working]          mastery, rune sockets, and prepared barrage
  barrage <working|off>        prepare automatic combat casting
  overchannel [off|5|10|20|25|30]
                                spend maximum SP for added spell power
  mageaura [style|off]         select a cosmetic prestige aura
  battlemage                   inspect FOCUS and AURA resonance
  runes [rune]                 known patterns and clues for sealed runes
  inscribe / unbind            change a working's rune bindings
  marginalia [style]           choose an Arcane 15 casting flourish
  showoff                      spend 3 SP on a prismatic armor flourish
  mage <message>               speak on the guild channel
  magi                         list visible Magi

Individual guide pages include:

  magehelp spells          working progression and combat relationships
  magehelp mastery         practice thresholds and socket progression
  magehelp runes           every rune and its compatible kinds of working
  magehelp barrage         automatic casting rules
  magehelp battlemage      FOCUS, AURA, and resonance
  magehelp overchannel     extra-SP settings and scaling
  magehelp marginalia      long-study cosmetic writing hands
  magehelp emotes          guild emotes

Use "help <command>" when you want the exact syntax of one ability.
Both "help tport" and "help teleport" open the travel working. Its fixed
destinations accept dw, hyper, souv, and vi as common shorthand.
